 {:seon.task/name "the-judge-reads-run-tests-results"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the prove re-review (2026-10-22): an agent's run carries clojure.test's report format end to end. `seon.agent/run-tests-here` collects each assertion as a report map (`seon.agent/test-report`), and the judge and the turn read them back through `seon.proofs/results`, `seon.proofs/red-reports`, `seon.proofs/failures`, `seon.proofs/run-errors` and `seon.proofs/costs`, while `seon.proofs/run-tests!` already answers one result per test ({:test :digest :pass :fail :error :ms}, a throw's :message and :data). Correct: the judge (`seon.reconcile/done-refusals`'s input), the turn (`seon.turn/observe`), the attempt's facts (:seon.attempt/failures, :seon.attempt/costs) and the context read run-tests!'s result map, with each red test's failing assertions (expected, actual, got) kept on its result; the report vector, `test-report` and the readers that rebuild a status per test from it go. About -30 lines in src. Proofs: the done refusal, the attempt's failures and costs, and the context's red block read the same from the result map as they do today from the reports."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.proofs/prove-runs-what-a-change-reaches"}}]
